MAJOR_VERSION=5
STANDARD_VERSION=3
RELEASE_VERSION=0
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=11
DESCRIPTION=Seven story slices. FL-22: the kernel workqueue grows delayed and periodic work (fl_wq_enqueue_at, fl_wq_enqueue_every, fl_wq_poll_at) held in a small time-ordered timer array and moved into the MLQ when due, FL_WQ_PROTECTED items that use a reserve of slots and run once at shutdown instead of being discarded, a nested-poll guard per queue instead of one global counter, and a per-queue mutex on hosted builds; the shell now starts a ticker thread (fl_bg_jobs_ticker_start) that is the only poller of the default queue, so fl_bg_jobs_tick is driven for the first time. The duplicate priority queue copies (repository root and src/) are deleted and the build uses kernel/core/sched/priority_queue.c. The browser image compiles the same queue sources (-DFL_FREESTANDING: no lock, a static item pool) and drives them from the PIT tick. Durable work (FL-25): fl_wq_enqueue_durable journals a job before accepting it, stages a bounded window into the queue, runs registered handlers by tag with retries, recovers at boot (cut-off work retried, stale work expired unrun, user-visible work held for its owner), and refuses with BUSY when the journal is full; the journal is an installable table, memory only by default and in the image, with a flushed SQLite backend for the hosted build. FL-17: CI now runs test_kq_checkpoint, test_kq_delivery, test_kq_net and test_kq_wire, and test_heritage pins that a 31-character account name is accepted, and test_freestanding_shell.py runs one scripted account session on the lab image and on the hosted shell and compares them. FL-04 (partial): session wire opcodes KQH_REQ 0x50 and KQH_DATA 0x51 in a second KeyQuorum range routed to the existing KeyQuorum hook, with invariant tests, and the history bundle framing (kernel/core/vfs/kq_history_bundle.[ch], two length-prefixed KQPB letters) with its own test; the host and client handlers are not built and a 0x50 or 0x51 frame is dropped until they are. FL-02 stage 1 (needs the KeyQuorum pin at 8ab454b, a commit on KeyQuorum's open pull request): the browser image links the KeyQuorum library built for x86_64-unknown-none and the existing driver (kq_platform.c: heap arena, RDRAND entropy that fails closed, CMOS UTC clock, the libc symbols the archive needs), prints CAP keyquorum=linked after the ABI probe, and the build refuses an image whose bss reaches the end of conventional memory; the delivery checkpoints are not in the image. FL-04 handlers: the host answers KQH_REQ through a gate and a source it is given (refusing visibly when either is missing), the client reassembles KQH_DATA into the two letters, with driver ops for the kind-17 snapshot and KQER error reports and the authz op codes 11 to 18 appended. FL-17 item 3: the bridge-reach assertion over kq_bridge_connects. FL-15 part A: the account store gains auth_mode, the account_keys / account_bridges / account_assembly tables and the KQST path accessor; the login hand-off to the key service is not built. FL-20 (absorbs FL-24): the KeyQuorum key service holds the signed-in account's signing key (opened by the login with its password, wiped at logout, never by su), runs on its own protected workqueue in a thread that cannot be cancelled or signalled, stamps a heartbeat the new P1-10 watchdog registry reads, runs the periodic signing sweep, and refuses the service-control authz op for every account; the Root fallback has no stored credential to read yet. Also: the CodeQL bundle is pinned so the register counts stay valid. Follow-up on this train: FL-25 safety (a failed RECOVER_ASK triage gates later polls so ASK work cannot stage without the owner, SQLite load/scan step errors are not reported as absence or OK, a failed durable load returns the claim and counts fl_wq_durable_load_failures, resolve_held and poll surface staging failures via the result / fl_wq_staging_errors, claim rollback unclaims before releasing the reservation), fl_bg_watchdog_clear so orderly service shutdown does not audit a false stall, docs/ROADMAP.md P1-8 prose aligned to contract rev 5, make test_workqueue_p18_tsan plus a CI step, and rustc -Vv recorded in c-cpp.yml (FL-17). FL-02 stage 2 remains blocked on owner entropy/RAM decisions and on repointing third_party/keyquorum after KeyQuorum #180 merges (pin is still ABI 3 while that PR is ABI 4). Also: FL-25 fault coverage for retry-table saturation, recovery after lost completion repairs, and a SQLite COMMIT refusal that rolls back the admit; test_workqueue_p18_tsan is in run_all_tests.sh. FL-25: ASK triage gate is per-executor (resolve allow-list); failed load that cannot return the claim increments stuck_claims; SQLite COMMIT failure still rolls back when the transaction remains open. Also: fl_wq_held_records error channel; real fl_wq_shutdown waits out in-flight claim rollback; SQLite COMMIT failure always ROLLBACKs. Also: fixed TSan race in shutdown-vs-claim test (condvar handoff under locks). Also: FL-22 acceptance evidence — freestanding build-info.json records payloadSectors/payloadBytes/bssEnd and conventionalMemoryBudget (browser-lab-build CI echoes and asserts them); FL-25 test that fl_wq_shutdown waits out resolve_held filler pins. Also: FL-15 open_account — fl_kq_open_account_secrets / fl_kq_open_account open a KQST through fl_kq_driver_t::slot_open with store pairing (fl_user_db_kqst_pairing); PASSWORD_KQST login publishes the signing secret through the session online_opened hook (fl_kq_service_online_opened; encryption secret wiped; box-key ownership still owner-blocked) with generation-checked rollback; refusal-matrix and su-restore signing tests; FL-22 hosted capacity/lock pin test plus CI Record FL-22 acceptance evidence step.

